[[File:RepublicTugboat-SWE.png|thumb|right|200px|A TUG-314 Republic tugboat]]
{{Quote|Looks like they're launching fighters.''"<br />"''They are not fighters, Commodore, more likely tugs.|Karyn Faro and [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]]|<ref name="Thrawn: Alliances">''[[Thrawn: Alliances]]''</ref>}}
'''Spacetugs''', also known as '''tugboats''', were utility [[Starship|spacecraft]] designed to assist in guiding larger vessels and their cargo in maneuvering through orbital transfer yards and transit corridors, by utilizing either [[tractor beam]]s or magnetic clamps.<ref name="ICS">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref>

During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]], as well as other agencies, employed at least two different models of [[TUG-314|specialized tugboats]] equipped with powerful tractor beams. They were used at both the [[Ord Cestus medical station]]<ref name="Brainz">{{TCW|Brain Invaders}}</ref> and [[space station]] [[Valor (space station)|''Valor'']].<ref name="No Return">{{TCW|Point of No Return (The Clone Wars)}}</ref> The warlike-[[species]] the [[Grysk]] utilized a [[Grysk tug|tug]].<ref name="Thrawn: Alliances" />

About thirty years after the [[Battle of Endor]], [[Sublights Products Corporation]] manufactured the [[TUG-b13|Quadrijet transfer spacetug]], which used magnetic clamps to quickly move around cargo containers.<ref name="ICS" /> One of these was present at [[Niima Outpost]] on [[Jakku]].<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref>

